I've done everything but priests and monks(lost a priest on astral :(  ), so
I'd say those are both really hard.  Priests have a really tough early game,
basically up until they can get a decent weapon.  Monks have it a little
easier, just because martial arts seems to work ok for the early game.
Hands down, monks have the hardest quest, so far I'm 1 for 3 vs. Master
Kaen, and the only time I  beat him I was using the staff of misspelling
(which goes against my normal artifactwishless conduct) (for reference, the
only other quest nemesis to kill any of my characters has been the Cyclops,
once, IIRC and I'm reading the logfile right)

Any class can be tough if you play them wrong, like I had a terrible time
with rangers until I actually started firing arrows and running away more.
Healers are also fairly tough early on, but gnomish healers are all set for
a protection racket.  Wizards are possibly tough until the quest, then they
are unstoppable.  Most of the fighter classes are varying degrees of easy,
with Valks or lawful arcs being really easy and cavemen probably being the
toughest.  So the hardest class would probably be something that can't
twoweapon

